THE any SHIM. This package carried the shim the pt2 rollout removed from 13 others:

    const defineExtension: typeof defineExtensionType = ((extension: any) => extension) as any;

Two any casts, and its justification comment asserted that 'standalone-installed extensions load only their own dist/, so @unbrained/pm-cli is not resolvable at runtime'. That premise is FALSE and was corrected upstream in pm-cli#717 — the SDK is importable at runtime wherever the package's own node_modules is populated.

Replaced with the fleet-standard helper, constrained by the SDK's own type so the extension object is contract-checked exactly as the imported helper would check it:

    const defineExtension = <TModule extends ExtensionModule>(module: TModule): TModule => module;

Kept type-only deliberately (import type from @unbrained/pm-cli/sdk/authoring). Reason is availability, not impossibility: a standalone-installed extension is not GUARANTEED a populated node_modules, so a value import would make activation depend on it. The EXIT_CODE comment was reworded to say that accurately instead of overclaiming.

Note the sdk/authoring subpath does not exist in 2026.7.25, which this package was pinned to — the host bump was a prerequisite, not a nicety.

THE NUL BYTE. index.ts contained a literal 0x00 character at line 1310, inside a composite dedupe key:

    const dedupeKey = `${target.webhookUrl}<NUL>${target.channel ?? ""}`;

The technique is sound — a NUL separator cannot collide with anything inside a URL or channel name, so it prevents ('ab','c') and ('a','bc') hashing alike. But writing it as a RAW BYTE rather than the \\u0000 escape made the whole 2104-line file binary: 'file' reported 'data', and grep -I (the default in most agent tooling, including Claude Code's wrapper) SILENTLY SKIPPED THE ENTIRE FILE. An agent searching this package for any symbol got zero hits and would reasonably conclude the code did not exist. For a project whose thesis is 'project management = context management', a source file invisible to search is a real defect. Replaced with the escape sequence: byte-identical at runtime, file is now plain UTF-8.
